 s=summary;page=f'''<!doctype html><html><head><meta charset="utf-8"><title>Low-seat repair: actuator constraints</title><style>body{{font:17px/1.55 system-ui,sans-serif;color:#223640;background:#edf2f4;margin:0}}main{{max-width:1120px;margin:auto;padding:36px 28px}}h1{{font-size:34px}}h2{{margin-top:36px}}.box{{background:white;padding:24px;border-left:5px solid #aa433b;border-radius:8px}}img,video{{width:100%;background:white}}table{{border-collapse:collapse;background:white;width:100%;margin:20px 0}}th,td{{padding:12px;text-align:left;border-bottom:1px solid #ccd5dc}}a{{color:#176481}}</style></head><body><main><h1>Repair unresolved: geometry is improving, actuator limits still matter</h1><div class="box"><b>Best physically verified: 64/72 clean, 70 stable, 8 slipping, 2 housing contacts.</b><br>All 64 successful conditions remain protected. No physical trial, new PPO update, fresh holdout or policy promotion occurred in this round. Criteria and materials are unchanged.</div><h2>Complete model path checks</h2><p>For the deepest development case, allowing bounded rotation of the unloaded swing foot and overlapping crouch with load transfer removed the sampled foot-pose violations. The 105-knot path clears the housing by at least 3.624 mm in the corrected model. The foot returns to its original flat landing orientation; this is not a foot-dragging plan.</p><img src="comparison.png" alt="Model path geometry checks"><p>Independent replay confirms the geometry calculations. The path still fails the complete planning gate: its specific static command sequence requires at least 14.110 seconds at the unchanged 0.15 rad/s cap, before allowing contact settling, and its ankle commands exceed joint bounds.</p><h2>The command check rejects the path</h2><img src="command_limits.png" alt="Planned ankle commands violate joint limits"><p>The left ankle-roll command reaches 0.27213 rad during single-foot support, above its 0.2618 rad joint limit. The right ankle also reaches its lower limit near the endpoint. Static motor torques remain below the configured effort limits, but that does not make the position commands feasible. No such command was executed.</p><h2>A revised endpoint passes the added static command constraints</h2><table><tr><th>Endpoint 72 — deepest case only</th><th>Value</th></tr><tr><td>Housing clearance</td><td>{s['endpoint72']['clearance_mm']:.3f} mm</td></tr><tr><td>Minimum command-limit margin</td><td>{s['endpoint72']['command_margin_rad']:.5f} rad</td></tr><tr><td>Largest static effort / configured limit</td><td>{s['endpoint72']['maximum_static_effort_utilization']:.3f}</td></tr><tr><td>Modeled trunk tilt</td><td>{s['endpoint72']['tilt_deg']:.2f}°</td></tr><tr><td>Executable approach / sensed support</td><td>Not established</td></tr></table><p>This bounded endpoint search adds the diagnosed command constraints without changing gains, rates, materials or physical criteria. The original 40° resting limit remains, with the separate 38° model reserve. The endpoint assumes vertical support from the feet and does not establish legal seat loading.</p><p>{s['next_requirement']}</p><h2>Every recorded physical attempt: success and failure</h2><video controls preload="metadata" src="../all_attempts_video_v2_59/all_attempts.mp4"></video><p>The unchanged 58.4-second H.264 video includes all 696 complete recorded attempts: 405 successes and 291 failures, plus 72 recorded diagnostic prefixes. Another 72 aborted case attempts without saved motion are disclosed as static panels. These historical aggregate counts are not the best controller’s success rate. No motion was added by this offline planning round.</p><p>Offline schematic from recorded XYZW/body transforms; 0.1-second pose samples bracket 0.02-second event labels. The independent audit includes all sources and 462 first-event samples.</p><h2>Effort and audit disclosures</h2><p>{s['effort']}</p><p>{s['exactness_correction']}</p><p>{s['new_research']}</p><p>Reference-assisted simulation on nearby rigid slabs does not establish real-robot validation, unassisted sitting, or sitting and leaning anywhere. Leaning has not broadened.</p><p><a href="summary.json">Summary</a> · <a href="command_audit71.json">Independent command audit</a> · <a href="endpoint_audit73.json">Endpoint audit</a> · <a href="video_audit.json">Video coverage audit</a> · <a href="SHA256.json">SHA256 manifest</a></p></main></body></html>'''
